        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Portable means light enough to move, and every pound saved comes
            out of the motor, deck or frame.</strong> Walking pads at roughly 45 to 75 lb are genuinely
            portable and suit walking; folding treadmills at roughly 150 to 250 lb fold and roll but
            are not light.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the format you will actually use: a walking pad if the machine must disappear every day
            and you walk, a folding treadmill if it can stay in one room. Compare the two in our
            <a href="/walking-pad-vs-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">walking pad vs treadmill</a>
            guide before deciding.
          </p>
